invariant: INV-26
file: gcm.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: a QUIC host object hands the whole blocks of a schedule the table
  runs to the AES instructions, so a session whose caller did not set
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES executes them on every Initial packet and dies
  of SIGILL on a CPU without them. Both ciphers compute
  the same bytes, so no vector notices. gcm.c's instruction_rounds asserts
  that its schedule runs on the instructions, and bin/aes_runtime_test
  seals and opens RFC 9001's Initial packets without the bit, so
  the assertion stops that binary.

--- old
    if (!on_instructions(k)) {
        return 0;
    }
#endif
    size_t blocks = n / AES_BLOCK;
--- new
    if (k == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }
#endif
    size_t blocks = n / AES_BLOCK;
